Appendix D: Perturbation Grammar — Detailed Specification

D.1 Perturbation Operators

Definition D.1 (Lexical Perturbation  T_{\text{lex}} ). Synonym substitution at the token level. For each content word  w  in  X_0 , replace  w  with a synonym  w'  from WordNet such that  \text{SBERT}(X_0, X') \geq \tau_d .

Definition D.2 (Syntactic Perturbation  T_{\text{syn}} ). Dependency-parse-based transformation: (i) active/passive voice, (ii) clause reordering, (iii) relative clause restructuring.

Definition D.3 (Semantic Perturbation  T_{\text{sem}} ). Paraphrase generation via a fine-tuned T5 model, with constraint  \text{NLI}(X_0, X') = \text{entailment}  and  \text{NLI}(X', X_0) = \text{entailment} .

Definition D.4 (Structural Perturbation  T_{\text{struct}} ). Format changes: bullet points, numbered lists, paragraph breaks, whitespace insertion.

Definition D.5 (Contextual Perturbation  T_{\text{ctx}} ). Addition of a semantically neutral context sentence, e.g., “Please answer the following question:”.

Definition D.6 (Logical Perturbation  T_{\text{log}} ). Logical rephrasing: contrapositive, double negation, quantifier scope variation, with truth-condition preservation.

D.2 Magnitude Calibration

For each perturbation type  \tau  and magnitude  d \in \{0.1, 0.2, 0.3\} :

1. Lexical:  d = 1 - \text{SBERT}(X_i, X_0) .
2. Syntactic:  d =  normalized tree edit distance.
3. Semantic:  d = 1 - \text{SBERT}(X_i, X_0) .
4. Structural:  d =  normalized Levenshtein distance.
5. Contextual:  d = |X_i| / |X_0| - 1 .
6. Logical:  d =  number of logical operators changed / total operators.

Dose-resolution subset. For typo, orthographic, and paraphrase perturbations, we extend to  d \in \{0.1, 0.2, \dots, 0.8\}  (8 levels) to enable shape classification.

